{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wMMaBUi1cRnmbELpHMxBj","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"combined_score\": 0.9192069392814439,\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"entrypoint_path\": \"src/program.py\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/investigation/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1\",\n  \"source_attempt_id\": \"c02_gated_domain_weighted_mondrian_attempt_01\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T09:37:08.741551+00:00\"\n}results/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\nresults/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1/src:\nprogram.py\n{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"The incumbent (class-conditional / confidence-bin Mondrian LAC split conformal, combined_score 0.868) is exact under exchangeability (marginal gap ~3e-4, controls passed) but its largest residual loss is most likely the shift cases: shift_coverage_gap ~0.061 is ~60% of alpha, which the 0.5*min(1, shortfall/alpha) term charges heavily, whereas set size (~0.166*0.25) and worst-slice gap (~0.05*0.25) contribute far less. Class-conditional calibration already neutralises pure label shift, so the remaining shift is plausibly covariate / confidence shift in the softmax outputs (e.g. temperature change, logit noise, degraded accuracy), which is visible in the UNLABELED test probabilities delivered by `predict`. Estimating a density ratio between calibration and test probabilities with a low-dimensional cross-fitted logistic domain classifier on sorted-probability summary features (max prob, margin, entropy, top-k log-ratios), and using it in per-test-row weighted Mondrian conformal (Tibshirani et al. 2019, test mass at +inf), will cut the shift-case undercoverage by at least a third while leaving exchangeable cases unchanged, because a positive-part (James-Stein) shrinkage factor beta = max(0, 1 - df/LR_stat) sets the log-weights to ~0 when the likelihood-ratio statistic of the domain classifier is at the null level. Expected: shift_coverage_gap falls from ~0.061 to <=0.04, mean_marginal_coverage_gap_exchangeable stays <= ~0.003, mean_set_size_ratio rises by at most ~0.01, so combined_score exceeds 0.868. Falsifier: if the shift in the evaluator is not detectable from test probs (e.g. pure label shift or shift only in P(y|x)), the gate keeps weights ~1 and the score equals the incumbent within noise; if the weights hurt exchangeable gap or set size by more than they help, revert to margin-only.\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c02_gated_domain_weighted_mondrian\",\n  \"implementation_plan\": [\n    \"Start from program_1/src/program.py (keep wire protocol: reset->{ok:true}, calibrate->{ok:true}, predict->{sets:MASK}; add no diagnostic keys). Keep class-conditional Mondrian for K<=10 and confidence-bin Mondrian for K>10, the LAC score, and the finite-sample level np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n.\",\n    \"In _finalize also store calibration summary features F_cal = _summary_features(probs): [max prob, top1-top2 log ratio, entropy, mean of top-5 log probs minus top-1 log prob, log K-normalised Gini], all computed from probs clipped at 1e-6; standardise with calibration mean/std. Dimension d<=6 so it is robust for K up to 100 and n_cal ~ 10^3.\",\n    \"At every predict call, accumulate unlabeled test features from all predict chunks seen so far (including the current one) and refit a ridge-penalised logistic domain classifier (calibration=0, test=1) by IRLS in numpy (_fit_domain_logistic, <=25 Newton steps, ridge 1.0, balanced class weights); each fit must take well under 1 s.\",\n    \"Compute the likelihood-ratio statistic LR = 2*(loglik_full - loglik_null) and the positive-part shrinkage beta = max(0, 1 - d / LR) in _positive_part_shrink; log-weight is beta * (logit(x) + log(n_cal / n_test_seen)) with the intercept term removed (weights are self-normalised), then clip w to [1/8, 8]. Under exchangeability LR ~ chi2_d so beta ~ 0 and w ~ 1. Cross-fit (2-fold over calibration rows and over test rows) so the weight of a calibration point is never produced by a model that saw that point.\",\n    \"Implement _weighted_group_thresholds(scores, weights, groups, n_groups, w_test, alpha): per group sort scores, form the weight cumsum cum_g, and for ALL test rows at once take idx = np.searchsorted(cum_g, (1 - alpha_g) * (W_g + w_test)) so each test row gets its own threshold with its own mass w_test at +inf (inf when idx >= n_g); the output q has shape [n_test, n_groups] and the mask is score_matrix <= q for K<=10 or the row's bin column for K>10. Preserve shrinkage toward the pooled weighted threshold with pseudo-count _SHRINK_N0.\",\n    \"Replace the fixed z-margin by an effective-sample-size margin: n_eff_g = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 within each group, alpha_g = max(alpha - z * sqrt(alpha*(1-alpha)*(1/n_eff_g + group_count_test_term)), 1e-6) with the same z as the incumbent (0.6/0.7); with beta=0 this must reproduce the incumbent thresholds exactly (add a self-check path / assertion-free fallback: if anything is non-finite, fall back to the incumbent unweighted thresholds).\",\n    \"Offline sanity study BEFORE finalising (local script outside the graded path is fine, not required in the deliverable): simulate softmax outputs for K in {5,10,30,100} with (i) exchangeable data, (ii) temperature shift T in {0.5,2}, (iii) logit noise shift, (iv) label-prior shift, (v) accuracy degradation; compare incumbent vs. new in coverage shortfall, worst-class/stratum gap, mean |set|/K over >=100 seeds with paired differences and a sign-flip test; tune only beta cap, weight clip and ridge on this simulator, not on any evaluator output.\",\n    \"Keep time per episode under ~3 s (limit 20 s per episode / call); seed any randomness from request['seed'] (reset) and never read evaluator files. Document limitations: weights are only identifiable for shift visible in probs; no guarantee for shift in P(y|x).\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_agent\": \"Interface (documented in program_0/src/program.py docstring): handle(request) with ops reset / calibrate (<=2 chunks, probs float32 [rows,K], labels, alpha, n_cal, n_test) / predict (<=4 chunks, unlabeled probs). Loss per episode = 0.5*min(1,max(0,1-alpha-coverage)/alpha) + 0.25*worst-slice undercoverage gap (classes if K<=10; set-size and max-prob strata if K>10) + 0.25*mean|set|/K; eligibility requires valid behaviour on three negative controls and marginal coverage near 1-alpha on exchangeable cases. Cycle-1 incumbent metrics: marginal gap 3e-4, set ratio 0.166, shift gap 0.061, worst-slice gap 0.050, controls 1.0. The shift-case coverage shortfall is therefore the main inferred lever (this decomposition is inferred from the aggregate metrics, the shift type is UNKNOWN; do not claim it). Design principle: any added mechanism must be an exact no-op (weights==1, thresholds identical to the incumbent) when the domain classifier finds no evidence of shift, so exchangeable cases and negative controls stay safe. Do not touch or read evaluator code; do not return extra keys. Only one harness evaluation per attempt, so validate locally with your own simulator first. If the local simulator shows weights do not help on any shift type, ship the incumbent plus only the ESS-based margin and state that honestly in the notes.\",\n  \"target_rubrics\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"combined_score > 0.8683476887134314\",\n      \"id\": \"incumbent_score_improvement\",\n      \"metric\": \"combined_score\",\n      \"operator\": \">\",\n      \"threshold\": 0.8683476887134314,\n      \"type\": \"metric\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The source implements a numpy ridge-logistic domain classifier on low-dimensional sorted-probability summary features (IRLS) and the positive-part shrinkage factor max(0, 1 - df/LR) that makes weights ~1 when no shift is detected.\",\n      \"id\": \"implementation_domain_classifier_weights\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"def _summary_features\",\n          \"def _fit_domain_logistic\",\n          \"def _positive_part_shrink\",\n          \"max(0.0, 1.0 -\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The source computes per-test-row weighted Mondrian thresholds with the test-point mass at +inf, via cumulative calibration weights and a vectorised np.searchsorted, plus an effective-sample-size margin and an unweighted fallback.\",\n      \"id\": \"implementation_per_row_weighted_mondrian\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"def _weighted_group_thresholds\",\n          \"np.cumsum(\",\n          \"np.searchsorted(cum\",\n          \"n_eff\",\n          \"np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Gated domain-classifier weighted Mondrian conformal\"\n}final.qualification.correct {'id': 'final.qualification.correct', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': True}\nfinal.qualification.outcome {'id': 'final.qualification.outcome', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': 'qualified'}\nfinal.qualification.status {'id': 'final.qualification.status', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': 'completed'}\nresult.best_correct_score {'id': 'result.best_correct_score', 'type': 'metric', 'value': 0.9192069392814439}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c54169c3-03e8-4441-993f-d5b8bf5939ea","uuid":"f16217c7-24e7-479d-9ac4-cd69b1c7b79f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:46:03.635Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"combined_score\": 0.9192069392814439,\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"entrypoint_path\": \"src/program.py\",\n  \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r02/claude/20261111_085834/investigation/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1\",\n  \"source_attempt_id\": \"c02_gated_domain_weighted_mondrian_attempt_01\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T09:37:08.741551+00:00\"\n}results/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\nresults/ideas/02_gated_domain_classifier_weighted_mondrian_conformal/program_1/src:\nprogram.py\n{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"The incumbent (class-conditional / confidence-bin Mondrian LAC split conformal, combined_score 0.868) is exact under exchangeability (marginal gap ~3e-4, controls passed) but its largest residual loss is most likely the shift cases: shift_coverage_gap ~0.061 is ~60% of alpha, which the 0.5*min(1, shortfall/alpha) term charges heavily, whereas set size (~0.166*0.25) and worst-slice gap (~0.05*0.25) contribute far less. Class-conditional calibration already neutralises pure label shift, so the remaining shift is plausibly covariate / confidence shift in the softmax outputs (e.g. temperature change, logit noise, degraded accuracy), which is visible in the UNLABELED test probabilities delivered by `predict`. Estimating a density ratio between calibration and test probabilities with a low-dimensional cross-fitted logistic domain classifier on sorted-probability summary features (max prob, margin, entropy, top-k log-ratios), and using it in per-test-row weighted Mondrian conformal (Tibshirani et al. 2019, test mass at +inf), will cut the shift-case undercoverage by at least a third while leaving exchangeable cases unchanged, because a positive-part (James-Stein) shrinkage factor beta = max(0, 1 - df/LR_stat) sets the log-weights to ~0 when the likelihood-ratio statistic of the domain classifier is at the null level. Expected: shift_coverage_gap falls from ~0.061 to <=0.04, mean_marginal_coverage_gap_exchangeable stays <= ~0.003, mean_set_size_ratio rises by at most ~0.01, so combined_score exceeds 0.868. Falsifier: if the shift in the evaluator is not detectable from test probs (e.g. pure label shift or shift only in P(y|x)), the gate keeps weights ~1 and the score equals the incumbent within noise; if the weights hurt exchangeable gap or set size by more than they help, revert to margin-only.\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"c02_gated_domain_weighted_mondrian\",\n  \"implementation_plan\": [\n    \"Start from program_1/src/program.py (keep wire protocol: reset->{ok:true}, calibrate->{ok:true}, predict->{sets:MASK}; add no diagnostic keys). Keep class-conditional Mondrian for K<=10 and confidence-bin Mondrian for K>10, the LAC score, and the finite-sample level np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n.\",\n    \"In _finalize also store calibration summary features F_cal = _summary_features(probs): [max prob, top1-top2 log ratio, entropy, mean of top-5 log probs minus top-1 log prob, log K-normalised Gini], all computed from probs clipped at 1e-6; standardise with calibration mean/std. Dimension d<=6 so it is robust for K up to 100 and n_cal ~ 10^3.\",\n    \"At every predict call, accumulate unlabeled test features from all predict chunks seen so far (including the current one) and refit a ridge-penalised logistic domain classifier (calibration=0, test=1) by IRLS in numpy (_fit_domain_logistic, <=25 Newton steps, ridge 1.0, balanced class weights); each fit must take well under 1 s.\",\n    \"Compute the likelihood-ratio statistic LR = 2*(loglik_full - loglik_null) and the positive-part shrinkage beta = max(0, 1 - d / LR) in _positive_part_shrink; log-weight is beta * (logit(x) + log(n_cal / n_test_seen)) with the intercept term removed (weights are self-normalised), then clip w to [1/8, 8]. Under exchangeability LR ~ chi2_d so beta ~ 0 and w ~ 1. Cross-fit (2-fold over calibration rows and over test rows) so the weight of a calibration point is never produced by a model that saw that point.\",\n    \"Implement _weighted_group_thresholds(scores, weights, groups, n_groups, w_test, alpha): per group sort scores, form the weight cumsum cum_g, and for ALL test rows at once take idx = np.searchsorted(cum_g, (1 - alpha_g) * (W_g + w_test)) so each test row gets its own threshold with its own mass w_test at +inf (inf when idx >= n_g); the output q has shape [n_test, n_groups] and the mask is score_matrix <= q for K<=10 or the row's bin column for K>10. Preserve shrinkage toward the pooled weighted threshold with pseudo-count _SHRINK_N0.\",\n    \"Replace the fixed z-margin by an effective-sample-size margin: n_eff_g = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 within each group, alpha_g = max(alpha - z * sqrt(alpha*(1-alpha)*(1/n_eff_g + group_count_test_term)), 1e-6) with the same z as the incumbent (0.6/0.7); with beta=0 this must reproduce the incumbent thresholds exactly (add a self-check path / assertion-free fallback: if anything is non-finite, fall back to the incumbent unweighted thresholds).\",\n    \"Offline sanity study BEFORE finalising (local script outside the graded path is fine, not required in the deliverable): simulate softmax outputs for K in {5,10,30,100} with (i) exchangeable data, (ii) temperature shift T in {0.5,2}, (iii) logit noise shift, (iv) label-prior shift, (v) accuracy degradation; compare incumbent vs. new in coverage shortfall, worst-class/stratum gap, mean |set|/K over >=100 seeds with paired differences and a sign-flip test; tune only beta cap, weight clip and ridge on this simulator, not on any evaluator output.\",\n    \"Keep time per episode under ~3 s (limit 20 s per episode / call); seed any randomness from request['seed'] (reset) and never read evaluator files. Document limitations: weights are only identifiable for shift visible in probs; no guarantee for shift in P(y|x).\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_agent\": \"Interface (documented in program_0/src/program.py docstring): handle(request) with ops reset / calibrate (<=2 chunks, probs float32 [rows,K], labels, alpha, n_cal, n_test) / predict (<=4 chunks, unlabeled probs). Loss per episode = 0.5*min(1,max(0,1-alpha-coverage)/alpha) + 0.25*worst-slice undercoverage gap (classes if K<=10; set-size and max-prob strata if K>10) + 0.25*mean|set|/K; eligibility requires valid behaviour on three negative controls and marginal coverage near 1-alpha on exchangeable cases. Cycle-1 incumbent metrics: marginal gap 3e-4, set ratio 0.166, shift gap 0.061, worst-slice gap 0.050, controls 1.0. The shift-case coverage shortfall is therefore the main inferred lever (this decomposition is inferred from the aggregate metrics, the shift type is UNKNOWN; do not claim it). Design principle: any added mechanism must be an exact no-op (weights==1, thresholds identical to the incumbent) when the domain classifier finds no evidence of shift, so exchangeable cases and negative controls stay safe. Do not touch or read evaluator code; do not return extra keys. Only one harness evaluation per attempt, so validate locally with your own simulator first. If the local simulator shows weights do not help on any shift type, ship the incumbent plus only the ESS-based margin and state that honestly in the notes.\",\n  \"target_rubrics\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"combined_score > 0.8683476887134314\",\n      \"id\": \"incumbent_score_improvement\",\n      \"metric\": \"combined_score\",\n      \"operator\": \">\",\n      \"threshold\": 0.8683476887134314,\n      \"type\": \"metric\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The source implements a numpy ridge-logistic domain classifier on low-dimensional sorted-probability summary features (IRLS) and the positive-part shrinkage factor max(0, 1 - df/LR) that makes weights ~1 when no shift is detected.\",\n      \"id\": \"implementation_domain_classifier_weights\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"def _summary_features\",\n          \"def _fit_domain_logistic\",\n          \"def _positive_part_shrink\",\n          \"max(0.0, 1.0 -\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"The source computes per-test-row weighted Mondrian thresholds with the test-point mass at +inf, via cumulative calibration weights and a vectorised np.searchsorted, plus an effective-sample-size margin and an unweighted fallback.\",\n      \"id\": \"implementation_per_row_weighted_mondrian\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"def _weighted_group_thresholds\",\n          \"np.cumsum(\",\n          \"np.searchsorted(cum\",\n          \"n_eff\",\n          \"np.ceil((n + 1) * (1 - alpha)) / n\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Gated domain-classifier weighted Mondrian conformal\"\n}final.qualification.correct {'id': 'final.qualification.correct', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': True}\nfinal.qualification.outcome {'id': 'final.qualification.outcome', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': 'qualified'}\nfinal.qualification.status {'id': 'final.qualification.status', 'type': 'final_qualification', 'value': 'completed'}\nresult.best_correct_score {'id': 'result.best_correct_score', 'type': 'metric', 'value': 0.9192069392814439}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
